            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance has now driven a “marathon” on Mars.** NASA reported that the rover reached the equivalent of **26.2 miles (42.195 km)** of driving after **about 5 years and 4 months** on the surface. An orbital image from Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter’s **HiRISE** camera captured Perseverance as a tiny speck and also shows the **winding tracks** it has carved across the terrain.【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance recently imaged Earth disappearing behind Phobos.** In a new sequence from **July 2, 2026** highlighted by NASA in early August, **Earth appears as a bright point** in the Martian sky and is seen **passing behind Mars’ moon Phobos** (an occultation) in images from Perseverance’s Mastcam-Z.【5:1†source】【5:3†source】\n\n- **Earlier in 2026: first AI-planned drive on another world.** NASA/JPL described a milestone demonstration where a **vision-capable generative AI** helped plan rover waypoints/routes, and Perseverance successfully executed those AI-generated plans on Mars (tests conducted in Dec. 2025; announced Jan. 30, 2026).【5:4†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest” as *last 7 days* vs *last month*, I can narrow this to the single most recent update and summarize it in one paragraph.",
